INT. SIGNAL BUNKER, MOUNTAIN PASS - NIGHT

A concrete cell the size of a freight elevator. One bare bulb. A field radio on a shelf, its dial glowing amber. Frost feathers the inside of a rifle slit.

CAPTAIN ISADORA REYES-WINTHROP (30s, grey streak in black hair, eyes like cold coins) sits on an ammo box with her boots off, rubbing her feet. Opposite her, LIEUTENANT KOFI ASANTE-BRIGGS (20s, still wearing his helmet, as if afraid to take it off) stares at the radio.

It hisses. A voice breaks through.

COMMAND (V.O.)
(over radio)
All stations, cease fire. Repeat, cease fire. It's over.

Neither moves.

KOFI
Captain?

ISADORA
I heard.

KOFI
Is it a trick?

ISADORA
Probably not.

She pulls her socks back on, slowly. He finally removes his helmet. His hair is wet with sweat.

COMMAND (V.O.)
(over radio)
Acknowledge, bunker seven.

Isadora lifts the handset, lets her thumb hover, and sets it down again.

ISADORA
Give me a minute.
